 axoplasm from squid giant axon</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1982</year><volume>218</volume><fpage>1129</fpage><lpage>1131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6183745</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="other">Bray, D. 1991. Isolated chick neurons for the study of axonal growth. <italic>In</italic> Culturing Nerve Cells. G. Banker and K. Goslin, editors. MIT Press, Cambridge,  MA. 119&#x02013;135.</citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bray</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunge</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Chapman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Geometry of isolated sensory neurons in culture. Effects of embryonic age and culture substratum</article-title><source>Exp  Cell Res</source><year>1987</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3780869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Visualization of single neurofilaments by immunofluorescence microscopy of splayed axonal cytoskeletons</article-title><source>Cell Motil Cytoskelet</source><year>1997</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>145</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9331218</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contiguous phosphorylated and non-phosphorylated domains along axonal neurofilaments</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><year>1998</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>455</fpage><lpage>467</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9443895</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-typ